 61CA    12C(82SE,X):NUC ID:XUNDL-1    2025TA21                           202511
 61CA c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2025Ta21:                          
 61CA2c  Physical Review C 112, 034604 (2025)                                   
 61CA c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL) October 11, 2025                 
 61CA c  Possible new nuclide identified in fragmentation of {+82}Se beam.      
 61CA c  E({+82}Se)=228 MeV/nucleon beam from the FRIB facility                 
 61CA2c   at MSU. The fragments were separated                                  
 61CA3c  and analyzed in the Advanced Rare Isotope Separator (ARIS).            
 61CA4c  Ions or fragments of interest were                                     
 61CA5c  detected in a PIN diode telescope of seven silicon detectors.          
 61CA6c  The |g-ray spectra were also measured                                  
 61CA7c  for identified particles via isomer tagging technique using            
 61CA8c  a HPGe detector.                                                       
 61CA  L  0                                                                    ?
 61CA2 L %B-=100                                                                
 61CA cL $Decay modes are not known. From theoretical Q values in 2019Mo01,     
 61CA2cL only possible decay mode is |b{+-},                                    
 61CA3cL thus 100% |b{+-} decay is assigned by inference                        
 61CA4cL by the compiler.                                                       
 61CA cL $1 event corresponding to {+61}Ca was identified (2025Ta21).           
 61CA2cL According to Feldman-Cousins method, at least two events are           
 61CA3cL required to obtain 90% confidence level for the existence of {+61}Ca.  

 61SC    9BE(76GE,X):NUCID:XUNDL-1     2009TA05                           200904
 61SC c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2009Ta05:                          
 61SC2c  Phys Rev Lett 102, 142501 (2009).                                      
 61SC c  Compiled by A. MacDonald and B. Singh (McMaster); April 9, 2009.       
 61SC c  {+61}Sc formed by fragmentation of {+76}Ge beam at 132 MeV/nucleon     
 61SC2c  at NSCL facility using A1900 fragment separator combined with S800     
 61SC3c  analysis beam line to form a two stage separator system. The           
 61SC4c  transmitted fragments were analyzed event-by-event in momentum and     
 61SC5c  particle identification. The nuclei of interest were stopped in eight  
 61SC6c  Si diodes which provided measurement of energy loss, nuclear charge    
 61SC7c  and total kinetic energy. The time-of-flight of each particle that     
 61SC8c  reached the detector stack was measured in four different ways using   
 61SC9c  plastic scintillators, Si detectors, and parallel-plate avalanche      
 61SCAc  counters. The simultaneous measurement of |DE signals, the magnetic    
 61SCBc  rigidity, total kinetic energy and the time-of-flight (tof) provided   
 61SCCc  unambiguous identification of the atomic number, charge state and mass 
 61SCDc  number.                                                                
 61SC  L 0                                                                      
 61SC cL $Measured cross section=8|*10{+-12} mb {i6} (read by compilers from    
 61SC2cL figure 2 of 2009Ta05).                                                 
 61SC cL E$ activity observed by 2009Ta05 is assumed to correspond to the       
 61SC2cL ground state of {+61}Sc.                                               

 61SC    12C(82SE,X):XUNDL-2           2026On01                           202606
