 61TI c  2019Wi04: E({+238}U)=345 MeV/nucleon. Many neutron-rich nuclei were    
 61TI2c  produced in the fragmentation of {+238}U beam. Fragments were          
 61TI3c  identified in mass number A, and A/Q (Q=charge) using magnetic         
 61TI4c  rigidity, tof, and energy loss (|DE-tof-B|r method) information in the 
 61TI5c  BigRIPS magnetic spectrometer. The ions of interest, in the present    
 61TI6c  case centered on {+64}V and {+60}Ti, were transported to the           
 61TI7c  ZeroDegree magnetic spectrometer, and implanted in the Advanced        
 61TI8c  Implantation Detector Array (AIDA) surrounded by the EURICA array      
 61TI9c  of 84 HPGe detectors at RIBF-RIKEN accelerator facility. Measured      
 61TIAc  correlated E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, delayed |g and half-lives of isomers.  
 61TIBc  Deduced levels, isomers, J|p, B(E2), B(M2). Comparison with large-scale
 61TICc  shell-model calculations.                                              
