 61FE    60FE(D,PG):XUNDL-6            2017GI03                           201704
 61FE c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Gi03:                          
 61FE c  Phys Rev C 95, 035806 (2017)                                           
 61FE c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL), April 26, 2017                  
 61FE c  {+60}Fe secondary beam at 27 MeV/nucleon was produced through          
 61FE2c  fragmentation of a {+64}Ni primary beam at 64.5 MeV/nucleon produced   
 61FE3c  at the Grand Acceleraueur d'Ions Lourds (GANIL) on a {+9}Be target     
 61FE4c  followed by separation with the LISE3 spectrometer.  The {+60}Fe beam  
 61FE5c  was incident on a 2.6 mg/cm{+2} Cd{-2} target. Measured Ep, |s(|q,p)   
 61FE6c  using a DSSSD detector (FWHH|?40-50 keV) and four telescopes of the    
 61FE7c  MUST2 array (FWHM |?80 keV). Measured E|g, I|g, proton-|g              
 61FE8c  coincidences using four segmented Clover detectors from the EXOGAM     
 61FE9c  array. Calculated |s(|q) and spectroscopic factors with ADWA           
 61FEac  calculations. Comparison with shell model calculations.                
 61FE cL E$Rounded values from the Adopted Levels of {+61}Fe in the ENSDF       
 61FE2cL database (March 2015 update)                                           
 61FE cL L,S$From comparison of d|s/d|W to ADWA calculations (2017Gi03)         
 61FE cL $Proton spectrum indicates a mixture of non-identified peaks between   
 61FE2cL 1300 and 1900 keV, however, lack of proton-|g coincidences did not     
 61FE3cL allow a determination of the exact states populated in this energy     
 61FE4cL region. In addition a broad peak at 3 MeV in the proton spectrum was   
 61FE5cL observed, however, no individual states could be identified. The       
 61FE6cL differential cross sections for 2-4 MeV proton energies                
 61FE7cL were fit using a combination of l=2                                    
 61FE8cL (d{-5/2}), l=3 (f{-5/2}) and l=4 (g{-9/2}) giving spectroscopic        
 61FE9cL factors of 0.69 {I20}, 0.10 {I19}, and 0.10 {I5}, respectively.        
 61FE cG E$Rounded values from the Adopted Gammas of {+61}Fe in the ENSDF       
 61FE2cG database (March 2015 update)                                           
