 61CO c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), May 4, 2015                           
 61CO c  Edited by B. Singh (McMaster), May 7, 2015                             
 61CO c  Multinucleon transfer in inverse kinematics                            
 61CO c  2015Ay02: E=275, 290 and 320 MeV {+48}Ca beams were produced from the  
 61CO2c  Argonne Tandem Linear Accelerator System (ALTAS). Target was a         
 61CO3c  self-supporting 0.973 mg/cm{+2} {+26}Mg. |g rays were detected with the
 61CO4c  Gammasphere 4|p array of 101 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors         
 61CO5c  surrounding the target and reaction residues were  analyzed with the   
 61CO6c  Fragment Mass Analyzer (FMA) and identified on event-by-event basis    
 61CO7c  from the position and time-of-flight measured in a microchannel plate  
 61CO8c  detector (MCP) placed at the focal plane and the energy loss measured  
 61CO9c  with a threefold segmented ionization chamber positioned behind the    
 61COac  focal plane. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q), |g|g(|q),           
 61CObc  Doppler-shift attenuation. Deduced levels, J, |p, bands, |g-ray        
 61COcc  multipolarities, quadrupole moment. Comparisons with shell-model       
 61COdc  calculations.                                                          
 61CO cG $Angular correlation ratio is defined as:                              
 61CO2cG R{-ac}=I|g(|q=forward/backword)/I|g(|q=90|'), with R{-ac}>1.0 for      
 61CO3cG stretched-quadrupole and <0.8 for stretched-dipole transitions         
 61CO4cG (2015Ay02).                                                            
