 61CO c  2024Aj01: E=43 MeV {+14}C beam was produced from the 9-MV tandem       
 61CO2c  accelerator at the John D Fox Laboratory of Florida State University.  
 61CO3c  Target was a thin foil of {+50}Ti with a thickness of around 500       
 61CO4c  |mg/cm{+2} (>90% enriched). |g rays were detected with the FSU         
 61CO5c  |g-detector array of six HPGe clover detectors with three coupled to   
 61CO6c  BGO shields and three single-crystal Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,  
 61CO7c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(DCO), |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J, |p, band         
 61CO8c  structures, |g-ray multipolarities. Comparisons with large-scale       
 61CO9c  shell-model calculations.                                              
