 61NI c  Ni isotopes were produced by 1.4 GeV proton pulses impinging on a      
 61NI2c  uranium carbide target at the CERN-ISOLDE.  Ni atoms effusing into     
 61NI3c  the ion source were ionized using in-source resonant laser ionization  
 61NI4c  with RILIS and then accelerated to 30 keV and 40 keV. The ions were    
 61NI5c  then mass-separated.  Magnetic and quadrupole moments were measured    
 61NI6c  using collinear laser spectroscopy. Comparison with {Iab initio} and   
 61NI7c  shell model calculations.                                              
