 61CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2010Vi07:                          
 61CU2c  Phys Rev C 82, 064311 (2010)                                           
 61CU c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), December 20, 2010                     
 61CU c  {+61}Cu was produced at ISOLDE-CERN facility by 1 GeV proton induced   
 61CU2c  fission of uranium carbide target. Resonance Ionization laser ion      
 61CU3c  source (RILIS) used to laser ionize the atoms followed by              
 61CU4c  high-resolution isotope separation (HRS) and ISCOOL Paul trap.         
 61CU5c  Measured hyperfine structure. Deduced spin, magnetic dipole moment and 
 61CU6c  electric quadrupole moment of the ground state. Collinear and in-source
 61CU7c  laser spectroscopic technique. Comparison with large-scale shell-model 
 61CU8c  calculations using {+56}Ni core.                                       
