 61ZN c  Compiled by J. Roediger and B. Singh (McMaster), February 28, 2005     
 61ZN c  E=104 MeV.  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g with the CLARION detector array,   
 61ZN2c  composed of ten clover detectors.  Each clover detector contains four  
 61ZN3c  Ge crystals, each of which is electrically twofold segmented.          
 61ZN c  The relative cross sections of the three A=61 isotopes {+61}Cu,        
 61ZN2c  {+61}Zn, and {+61}Ga are estimated from the known or presumed          
 61ZN3c  ground state transitions to be 420:110:1, respectively, in 2005An03.   
 61ZN cG $R{-154-90}=Y(154|')/Y(90|'), where Y(|q) represents the |g-ray        
 61ZN2cG yield at one of the detector rings of CLARION. Ratios for known        
 61ZN3cG stretched |DJ=2 reference transitions amount to roughly 1.6-1.7, while 
 61ZN4cG stretched |DJ=1 transitions have R{-154-90} equal to |?0.7-0.8.        
