 61ZN c  Compiled by: M. Mitchell and B. Singh (McMaster), Nov 30, 2006.        
 61ZN c  E=104 MeV. Measured E|g, |g|g, I|g, |g(|q) using the CLARION Ge        
 61ZN2c  detector array, and the Recoil Mass Spectrometer (RMS). The CLARION    
 61ZN3c  array was comprised of ten Ge 'Clover' detectors placed in a three     
 61ZN4c  ring configuration at 90|', 132|', and 154|' with respect to the beam  
 61ZN5c  direction. Large-scale shell-model calculations                        
 61ZN c  Comparison of experimental and theoretical branching ratios are given  
 61ZN2c  in Table 2 of 2006An31 using shell-model calculation.                  
 61ZN cG $ R{-154|',96|'}=Yield at 154|'/Yield at 96|'. Typical values are      
 61ZN2cG 1.6-1.7 for |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions and 0.7-0.8 for |DJ=1,       
 61ZN3cG dipole transitions                                                     
